<title>USA: ADM to cut board to 12, add 3 outsiders.</title>
<headline>ADM to cut board to 12, add 3 outsiders.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Archer Daniels Midland Co, the agricultural products company, said Monday it proposed to reduce the number of its directors to 12 from 17 and add three outside directors to a management slate.</p>
<p>In a proxy statement filed with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission, ADM chairman Dwayne Andreas said in a letter to stockholders the current board took into consideration a 1996 study on independent directors.</p>
<p>&quot;And we will endeavor to maintain the proper ratio of inside and outside directors,&quot; Andreas said.</p>
</text>
